==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-make sense.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-make sense.ogg|a=Mid-Atlantic US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,made>}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|idiomatic}} To be [[sensible]], [[coherent]], [[reasonable]].
#: {{syn|en|add up|figure|track|check out}}
#: {{ux|en|The thing doesn’t '''make sense''' to me.}}
#: {{ux|en|Somehow the combination didn’t '''make sense''', but Cranston took it at face value, whatever that was worth.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2025 February 19|author=Paul Clifton|title=I am absolutely committed to reforming the railway|journal=RAIL|issue=1029|page=41|text=Hendy has come out as something of an evangelist for discontinuous electrification. For Waterloo-Exeter, this could '''make''' real '''sense''' on a route where the high capital cost of wiring or [[third rail]] all the way to Devon would be prohibitive. But what about his vocal support for it on East West Rail, which is effectively a brand new line?}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|idiomatic|with {{l|en|of}}}} To [[decipher]] or [[understand]].
#: {{syn|en|make head or tail of}}
#: {{ux|en|Can you '''make sense''' of her handwriting?}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{non-gloss|Used to express interest or desire in something}}; to be pleasing or beneficial; to [[work]], be [[operative]], or be [[advantageous]] to.
#: {{usex|en|Maybe we should take a break. I mean, our relationship just isn't '''making''' much '''sense''' anymore.}}
# {{cln|en|negative polarity items}} {{lb|en|generally negated|bodybuilding|_|slang}} To be in the [[realm]] of the [[ordinary]], to be not [[particularly]] [[developed]].
#: {{ant|en|ridiculous|absurd|Thesaurus:strapping}}
#: {{ux|en|If you want to grow spinal erectors that '''don’t make sense''', you have to do a lot of bent-over compound lifts.}}

